      "side": 1,
      "message": "Can you use skslc and compile_sksl_tests to generate \"golden\" htmls for the visualizer output of a few simple inputs?\n\nIf you want real unit tests, you could also make a few tests that look for expected snippets within the HTML, instead of checking the entire HTML string at once. e.g. \n\n  // run visualizer on simple input\n  REPORTER_ASSERT(r, strstr(myHTML, \"\u003cb\u003eexpected_op v1 \u003d 234\u003c/b\u003e\");",
